From bdfc49086f86c62ff1af3059b498843bd7f56182 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 09:09:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: PDF markup-injection crashes across the entire PDF
 module (systemic, not isolated)

Root cause (same class as the earlier diagram-crash fix, but far more
widespread): AI-generated text was being embedded raw into ReportLab's
Paragraph markup (a small XML-like tag language) throughout every PDF
section file, with no escaping anywhere. Any '&', '<', or '>' in
AI-generated content -- plausible in almost any field ("AI & ML
Platform", "cost < $50/mo", "<Container> component") -- corrupts
or crashes the markup parser. This is what produced:

    paragraph text '<para><font size="18"></para>' caused exception
    Parse error: saw </para> instead of expected </font>

on project 15's title. Rather than patch that one field, audited and
fixed every place across all 8 PDF section files that embeds raw
AI-generated text into markup:

- src/pdf/components.py: added safe_text() (escapes a value for safe
  Paragraph embedding) and collapse_ws() (normalizes incidental
  whitespace/newlines in multi-line f-string templates so they don't
  get misread as content row-breaks). Applied safe_text() to every
  shared low-level helper (title, section_title, subsection, body,
  muted, bullet, code, create_metric_card, create_tag) so escaping
  happens centrally. create_card()'s heading argument is now escaped
  unconditionally -- no call site ever legitimately needs markup in a
  heading, so this is safe with zero double-escaping risk.
- executive_summary.py, architecture.py, planner.py, judge.py,
  metadata.py, appendix.py, pitch.py, cover.py: wrapped every raw
  AI-generated value passed into create_card()/Paragraph() with
  safe_text() -- titles, taglines, problem/solution statements,
  feedback, bullet-list items, competitor names, team roles, the
  project idea, everything.
- Self-caught regression: an intermediate version of this fix made
  create_card() also split on plain newlines as a blanket safety net,
  which broke call sites using multi-line f-string templates purely
  for source-code readability (tore a single logical tag apart across
  rows -- the exact same 'unclosed tag' error this fix exists to
  prevent, just self-inflicted). Reverted create_card() to only split
  on the deliberate '<br/>' convention, and used the new collapse_ws()
  helper at the two call sites (executive_summary's hero card,
  metadata's Project Identity card) that needed their incidental
  newlines normalized instead.

Verified: a comprehensive adversarial test loading '&', '<', '>' into
EVERY field simultaneously (title, tagline, problem, solution,
features, diagram, competitors, feedback, team roles, everything)
generates successfully; visually confirmed via rendered PNG that the
characters display as literal text, not corrupted; reran the existing
clean-data PDF test and the full 5-stage workflow integration test to
confirm no regression on the normal path.
